Scaffold a Solidity snippet that accurately verifies Merkle proof for a given hash root, using leaf nodes and proof elements. The contract should include a library function 'MerkleProof' containing the 'verify' function, which recursively aggregates hashes using keccak256. Implement a hash computation logic within the function while ensuring that the input arrays of proof and leaf nodes are correctly iterated. Additionally, test the smart contract using a Merkle tree with multiple levels, including nodes with unique leaf values and proof elements.

```solidity
// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
pragma solidity >=0.6.0 <0.8.0;
library MerkleProof {
    function verify(bytes32[] memory proof, bytes32 root, bytes32 leaf) internal pure returns (bool) {
        bytes32 computedHash = leaf;
        for (uint256 i = 0; i < proof.length; i++) {
            bytes32 proofElement = proof[i];
            if (computedHash <= proofElement) {
                // Hash(current computed hash + current element of the proof)
                computedHash = keccak256(abi.encodePacked(computedHash, proofElement));
            } else {
                // Hash(current element of the proof + current computed hash)
                computedHash = keccak256(abi.encodePacked(proofElement, computedHash));
            }
        }
        // Check if the computed hash (root) is equal to the provided root
        return computedHash == root;
    }
}
