Outline a solution that reads an address from a position in a byte array. Implement a function that takes a byte array and an index as inputs, then checks if the length of the byte array is sufficient for the read operation. If the length is incorrect, revert the transaction with an error. Otherwise, read the address from the byte array and return it. The function should use assembly language to load the 32-byte word from memory and apply a 20-byte mask to obtain the address.

```solidity
pragma solidity 0.7.5;
import "./LibBytesRichErrors.sol";
import "./LibRichErrors.sol";
library LibBytes {
    using LibBytes for bytes;
    /// @dev Reads an address from a position in a byte array.
    /// @param b Byte array containing an address.
    /// @param index Index in byte array of address.
    /// @return result address from byte array.
    function readAddress(bytes memory b,
        uint256 index)
        internal
        pure
        returns (address result)
    {
        if (b.length < index + 20) {
            LibRichErrors.rrevert(LibBytesRichErrors.InvalidByteOperationError(LibBytesRichErrors.InvalidByteOperationErrorCodes.LengthGreaterThanOrEqualsTwentyRequired,
                b.length,
                index + 20 // 20 is length of address));
        }
        // Add offset to index:
        // 1. Arrays are prefixed by 32-byte length parameter (add 32 to index)
        index += 20;
        // Read address from array memory
        assembly {
            // 1. Add index to address of bytes array
            // 2. Load 32-byte word from memory
            // 3. Apply 20-byte mask to obtain address
            result := and(mload(add(b, index)), 0xffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffff)
        }
        return result;
    }
}
